<!-- Cover: uses all five slots of the title layout, and **no alignment at all** — placement belongs to
     the theme's title.slots.css. This deck renders with the dark built-in theme `ink` (balpyo.json) —
     a postmortem is watched together on one screen in a dimmed room.

     **This deck's color rule** — only three of the six accents are used, each with exactly one meaning:

       - `accent5` (red) = **what the incident cost** — duration, error rate, the start of the incident.
       - `accent4` (amber) = **where we were late** — time to detect.
       - `accent3` (green) = **what we did and will do** — mitigation and actions.

     Blue (`accent1`) does not appear. With a single color all you can say is "this matters"; what
     matters in a postmortem is **which part is damage and which part is response**. The same reason caps
     the palette at three: a fourth meaning would make the audience memorize a legend. The 47 min on the
     cover is the rule's first use. -->
<slide id="cover" layout="title" enter="rise">
  <text slot="kicker" variant="kicker" color="accent5">Incident review · INC-2431 · SEV-2</text>
  <text slot="title" role="title" size="80">Payments API 5xx, <span color="accent5">47 min</span></text>
  <text slot="subtitle" role="heading" size="30" color="muted">A cache stampede — what happened and what we change</text>
  <text slot="author" role="body">Platform Team</text>
  <text slot="date" role="caption" color="muted">2026-09-18 · Blame the system, not people</text>
  <note>Ground rule first: we look at the system, not at people. Thirty seconds.</note>
</slide>
